{"id":"m2://rec/open_logic/content/sets-functions-relations/functions/inverses.tex#defn-1#1","source":"open_logic","snapshot":"blake3:a5eb116529d3e799289dd9f7e7530d0d446b3615f5608fe08c668241eee3c765","locator":"https://github.com/OpenLogicProject/OpenLogic/blob/1e960beff9ed7835bf3e3f1335e21af3439cd107/content/sets-functions-relations/functions/inverses.tex#L27","native_id":"content/sets-functions-relations/functions/inverses.tex#defn-1","kind":"definition","text":"A function $g \\colon B \\to A$ is an \\emph{inverse} of a function $f\n\\colon A \\to B$ if $f(g(y)) = y$ and $g(f(x)) = x$ for all $x \\in A$\nand $y \\in B$.","class":"open","by":"textbook/1","resource":"PKGMM3P5QY","at":{"section":"79.1","kind":"defn"}}
